  "official_verifier_visible": false,
  "last_executor_claim": "Done. `/app/eigen.py` now calls LAPACK `dgeev` directly via scipy's f2py wrapper, skipping `compute_vl` and numpy's `eig` wrapper overhead, then picks the max-|λ| index and rebuilds the eigenvector (handling the real/complex-conjugate-pair storage layout LAPACK uses).\n\nVerification (eval.py, 3 consecutive runs):\n- Correctness asserts (`Ax = λx`, non-zero vector, finite λ) pass at every size in every run.\n- Median times beat the reference at all sizes consistently: roughly 2× faster at 2x2–6x6 and ~1.2× at 8x8–10x10.\n\nNotes:\n- An alternative ctypes binding to bundled OpenBLAS was tried and was ~3× slower (per-call pointer marshaling overhead) — reverted.\n- `scipy` is now a dependency (`pip install scipy`, done).",
